  ('d3b04742-de8b-59a5-9618-b5519cb73260', 'GA', 'state', null, 'Official Code of Georgia Annotated (free public access) — Title 44, Chapter 7: Landlord and Tenant', 'https://www.lexisnexis.com/hottopics/gacode/', 'State of Georgia via LexisNexis (the link is on the Georgia General Assembly website)', 'state_legislature', 'statute', array['general','repairs_habitability','security_deposit','eviction','retaliation','lease_termination']::text[], 'both', 'other', 'The State of Georgia''s free public-access edition of the Official Code of Georgia Annotated; the landlord-tenant provisions are in Title 44, Chapter 7.', 'O.C.G.A. Title 44, Chapter 7 (§ 44-7-1 et seq.)', null, 'unverifiable', 'The URL is live. It returns a 301 to LexisNexis Advance''s free public-access ''container'' page (HTTP 200). That page is a JavaScript and cookie-fingerprinting shell, so an automated fetch shows no text, and the code content and Title 44 Ch. 7 could not be seen directly. Web search was out of budget, so I checked the publisher a different way. I downloaded the Georgia General Assembly site''s own JS bundle (legis.ga.gov, main.f3b17f83c46a0b38a9be.js). Its footer under ''Georgia Laws & Government'' has a ''Georgia Code'' link pointing to exactly http://www.lexisnexis.com/hottopics/gacode. That confirms the link is the legislature''s official pointer to the free OCGA. Keep the original hottopics URL rather than the advance.lexis.com config URL, because the config token can change. Caveats: (1) the link opens the whole OCGA, not Title 44 Ch. 7 directly, so users have to browse to it, and the title should not suggest a deep link; (2) LexisNexis may show a terms-of-use acceptance before the code; (3) the publisher label is accurate: the State of Georgia''s official code, hosted by LexisNexis. Check it once by hand in a browser before shipping.', '2026-10-19T00:00:00Z', '{"notes":"Checked this session. The Georgia General Assembly site (legis.ga.gov) has a footer link labelled \"Georgia Code\" under \"Georgia Laws & Government\". It points to this exact URL; that was found in the site''s JavaScript bundle (main.f3b17f83c46a0b38a9be.js). Opening the URL returns a 301 redirect to https://advance.lexis.com/container?config=00JAAzZDgzNzU2ZC05MDA0LTRmMDItYjkzMS0xOGY3MjE3OWNlODIKAFBvZENhdGFsb2fcIFfJnJ2IC8XZi1AYM4Ne, which returns HTTP 200. That page is a JavaScript app that needs cookies, so the statute text itself could not be read. For that reason fetched is set to false. The URL does not link to Chapter 44-7 directly: users have to browse to Title 44 > Chapter 7 after accepting the terms."}'::jsonb),
