  ('3c972a99-3529-5eaf-97b9-87335850a230', 'ID', 'state', null, 'Idaho Code 55-306 - Local Government - No Rent Control', 'https://legislature.idaho.gov/statutesrules/idstat/Title55/T55CH3/SECT55-306/', 'Idaho Legislature', 'state_legislature', 'rent_regulation', array['rent_control']::text[], 'both', 'html', 'Official text of Idaho Code 55-306, which prohibits local governments from regulating rent, fees or deposits on private residential rental property.', 'Idaho Code 55-306', '2025', 'unverifiable', 'legislature.idaho.gov refused the connection. Search returned this exact URL, and the snippet confirms the title ''Local Government — no rent control'', added in 2025 (ch. 65, sec. 6). It bars local units from enacting or enforcing ordinances that regulate rent, fees or deposits for private residential leasing, or that would effectively force owners into an optional federal housing assistance program. The description leaves out that second clause (a voucher/source-of-income mandate ban), which would be worth adding. Note that the July 2026 AG manual appendix does not list 55-306, and its 55-307 is now ''Removal of fixtures by tenant''.', '2026-10-19T00:00:00Z', '{"notes":"Official site refused automated connection; URL and 2025 history note (ch. 65, sec. 6) confirmed via web search."}'::jsonb),
