  ('c5b85e0f-c1ed-5b06-be8d-1cdf8447d505', 'WI', 'state', null, 'Wis. Stat. 66.1015 - Local regulation of residential rental property (rent control preemption)', 'https://docs.legis.wisconsin.gov/document/statutes/66.1015(1)', 'Wisconsin State Legislature', 'state_legislature', 'rent_regulation', array['rent_control','rent_increase']::text[], 'both', 'html', 'Statute subsection prohibiting local governments from regulating the amount of rent or fees for private residential rental property.', 'Wis. Stat. 66.1015(1)', null, 'unverifiable', 'Host unreachable, and no search was possible. Wisconsin Law Help''s ''All About - Rent Increases and Late Fees'' cites Wis. Stat. 66.1015(1) as barring local governments from limiting rent, and DATCP''s tenant fact sheet says ''There are no state laws limiting the amount of a rent increase.'' The formal section heading could not be confirmed, so the title''s wording ''Local regulation of residential rental property'' is unverified.', '2026-10-19T00:00:00Z', '{"notes":"URL linked from WisLawHelp, which cites it for the statement that local governments cannot limit rent. Official site unreachable this session."}'::jsonb),
